<title>MEXICO: RESEARCH ALERT-Empresas ICA upgraded.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Empresas ICA upgraded.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>UBS Securities said it upgraded construction firm Empresas ICA (ICA) to buy from hold.</p>
<p>Analyst Alvaro Shirashi said recent falls in the share price created a buy opportunity since ICA had attractive valuations and strong earnings growth.</p>
<p>&quot;Recent price weakness created a window of opportunity to play the expected recovery of the Mexican construction industry through the safest vehicle available,&quot; Shirashi wrote.</p>
<p>Shirashi said he projected earnings per ADR to grow 77 percent in 1997 against consensus two percent EPS growth for the Mexican stock index.</p>
<p>UBS's 12-month price target for the ADR was $18, which it said indicated a 30 percent upside.</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom +525 728 7907</p>
</text>
